      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T19:00:35Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the live Ethereum transaction, receipt and call trace, the pair's CREATE2 deployment trace, pre-exploit runtime, verified source, exact commit-matching source snapshot, protocol post-mortem, and reported bad debt. The exploit transaction creates the attack contract, which calls borrow(10,000,000e18,0,receiver) on 0x6e90c85a495d54c6d7e1f3400fef1f6e59f86bd6. During that call the pair's configured oracle returns 2000000000000000000001998001998001998; the pair's own 1e36/price operation rounds to zero and its own LTV multiplication therefore passes solvency. The empty configured vault makes the oracle input manipulable, but the defect is the pair runtime's accepted zero rate and unsafe solvency use. The target is a full direct runtime with no DELEGATECALL or SELFDESTRUCT, created in the recorded deployment transaction and unchanged through the exploit. Resupply reports $10 million of reUSD bad debt, matching the exact onchain borrow amount."
    }
